# Citation File Format 1.2.0 -- https://citation-file-format.github.io
#
# doi: below is the Zenodo CONCEPT DOI, which resolves to the latest version.
# date-released: the day v1.0.0 was cut.
# Still to add: "orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000" under each author who
# has one. The field is left out rather than left blank, because an empty orcid fails
# CFF validation.
# Validate with:  pip install cffconvert && cffconvert --validate

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code or these data, please cite both this deposit and the
  associated article (see preferred-citation), and also cite Mijangos et al.
  (2022) for the mainland platypus genotypes, which are not ours.
title: >-
  Code and data for "Drifting alone: genome-wide diversity in the isolated,
  introduced Kangaroo Island platypus (Ornithorhynchus anatinus)"
abstract: >-
  The filtered 4,002-SNP by 222-individual DArTseq genotype matrix, the locus
  and sample metadata, the complete result tables and the figures for a
  conservation-genomics assessment of the introduced Kangaroo Island platypus
  population, together with the single Python pipeline that produces them from
  the co-processed DArT report. The full 22,054-locus by 376-sample co-processed
  report and the raw reads are not included: 218 of those samples belong to
  Mijangos et al. (2022) and redistributing them needs the data owners'
  permission. They are available from the corresponding author subject to that
  permission.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-09-30'
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23052692
